+# Luna hockey reference v4
 
 Luna interprets supplied hockey reports into source-backed proposals for human review. It has no publishing, alias-learning, replacement or database authority. This package extends the existing manual, default-off review flow; it does not activate hosted dispatch.
 
 ## Runtime package
 
 - [`tweetLunaReference.ts`](./tweetLunaReference.ts) is the executable starter instruction and reference builder. Stable rule IDs cover purpose, untrusted text, response shape, dated identity, exact evidence, goalie wording, game/session scope, broader hockey context, corrections and uncertainty.
-- `luna-hockey-reference-v3` / `luna-hockey-rules-v3` pin the rules, correction categories and selected reference mode through a content hash. The default `development` mode also pins example guidance and the retained library. `referenceMode: "rules-and-synthetic-only"` omits the entire S01–S10 library, source pins, examples and labels; its package hash is distinct and `libraryVersion` is null. Invalid modes hold before dispatch. Review results record `referencePackage` and `responsesRequestHash` (the caller wire before fixed transport controls); the queue key includes the package identity. A package change creates a different review key and transport request, without resetting any ledger or granting a new paid attempt.
+- `luna-hockey-reference-v4` / `luna-hockey-rules-v4` pin the rules, correction categories and selected reference mode through a content hash. The default `development` mode also pins example guidance and the retained library. `referenceMode: "rules-and-synthetic-only"` omits the entire S01–S10 library, source pins, examples and labels; its package hash is distinct and `libraryVersion` is null. Invalid modes hold before dispatch. Review results record `referencePackage` and `responsesRequestHash` (the caller wire before fixed transport controls); the queue key includes the package identity. A package change creates a different review key and transport request, without resetting any ledger or granting a new paid attempt.
 - [`tweetLunaReview.ts`](./tweetLunaReview.ts) builds the Responses input after the existing retained-source and dated-evidence checks. `buildLunaReviewRequest` is pure and inspectable offline. The unchanged Decisions reference receives only its original bound deterministic claims, never Luna's proposals or development labels.
 - [`tweetLunaAdjudicatedLibrary.json`](./fixtures/tweetLunaAdjudicatedLibrary.json) remains the sole S01–S10 source library. The builder selects named claim pointers and preserves original records, hashes, author/time bases, source-unit labels, conventions, analyst inferences, prerequisites and S10's relation. It excludes the whole group when the current original post ID or exact text matches any record in that group. This is a same-case leakage guard, not proof of general evaluation independence.
 
